{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3163","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3163","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3163\",\"parent_revision\":\"1454d8148ac559978b510a25f1d1c0edf6398e029f66fcfb734db8eeccb3c249\",\"root_revision\":\"1454d8148ac559978b510a25f1d1c0edf6398e029f66fcfb734db8eeccb3c249\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`skills/task-decomposition/SKILL.md` cites `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` by a repository-relative path.\\n\\nThat path resolves only in a checkout of this repository. In an install the working directory is the consuming project's root, so the reference points at a file that is not there. A skill body is shipped content read by an agent in whatever install it lands in.\\n\\nObserved while correcting the plan-file authoring model in the same file.\\n\\nThis is the same class as the agent-file path problem already established: shipped content cannot rely on paths relative to its own location or to this repository. The reliable form is naming a skill to load.\\n\\nWorth a sweep rather than a single fix \u2014 one instance found incidentally suggests others, and a repo-relative path in shipped content fails silently by pointing at nothing rather than erroring.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-23, while correcting task-decomposition\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a83d7bc359cfd6de57e0f6fb105e86889ccba8ca4927f05d4055c78e9b3ec050\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQN34FA\"}"}